 why we here  today before we get into the moral  structure of Coos ins character though I  first want to quickly update you guys on  our small challenge we've had recently  once again you have  bb2 it and reached a 3,000 light mark on  the last video a lot faster than I  anticipated to shape so this time we're  gonna raise the bar to 3,500 likes in  the very first 24 hours that this video  is online and you will get the second  Admiral by next Tuesday and by the way  if you're wondering why in the world is  this guy trying to get more likes on his  videos it's because one it makes these  videos a lot more available to more  people and two it really motivates me  like crazy to work more consistently to  give you guys not only more but also  better content so smash the like button  and make me work but enough about that  after all we're here to delve into one  of the most philosophical questions in  the entirety of storytelling so let's  take a look at the man who is so chill  that he thinks justice should be lazy  okichi cruisin is one of the most  popular members of the Marines that most  of the time acts as an antagonistic  force to Luffy and his crew he's a tall  slender and muscular Lee build man with  long curl back hair and tan skin despite  being the youngest among the admirals by  quite a bit he nonetheless is without a  doubt one of the strongest characters in  the story thanks to years of hard  training as well as his powerful logia  devil fruit that turns his entire body  into ice having joined the ranks of the  Marines at a very young age  Alki G has worked his way up the ranks  fairly quickly which is no big surprise  as we know he can be very determined and  focused when he needs to in general  however alka G is a rather laid-back  person that enjoys respect and  popularity throughout the ranks of the  Marines this is most likely not only due  to his immense strength and influence  but also due to his personality which is  unusually kind and respectful compared  to other high-ranking members as a  matter of fact respect and fairness are  two of the most defining traits for  qoodles personality not only does he  treat his fellow Marines respectfully  and fair but he even acknowledges  alleged criminals for doing good deeds  a great example for this is letting  luffy and the crew go free  not only for taking down the tyrannical  crocodile and liberating alabasta but  also out of respect for Luffy's will to  sacrifice himself for his crew what  makes our ki ji a truly good character  in the eye of the reader however is that  his respectfulness and fairness are  firmly grounded in the empathy and  compassion he feels for others he takes  people circumstances and their good  intentions into account and wants to  help create a world with less suffering  and pain we can see this for instance  when he freezes the entire ocean only to  let on she'd returned to his clan after  the events at the Davi back fight but I  think nothing proves this point quite as  well as his relationship with Robin even  though he was tasked with tracking her  down and capturing her he was genuinely  relieved and happy that she had finally  found true friends all of that despite  the straw hats just having invaded  Anna's Lobby and having declared war  against the world government itself  okichi however is very aware of Robins  true personality and how she had no  fault at becoming a criminal in the eyes  of the world which is exactly why he  allowed her to flee the slaughter of her  Island many years ago in the first place  you may ask yourself now how someone  this caring and apparently soft could  possibly become an admiral in the  otherwise so hard-boiled Marines as a  matter of fact many of the Marines asked  themselves the same question but the  answer to that is quite simple Kuzon has  an incredibly strong sense of duty even  though he allows himself to live  according to his morals most of the time  when it's expected of him he's always  ready to follow orders and do what's  expected of him as an admiral during the  war at marine fort for example he  grudgingly drops his usually laid-back  and friendly nature and trades it for a  more  an unforgiving personality and we can  also see this when he first encounters  Robin and the straw heads for the first  time where he had first decides to leave  them alone before changing his mind and  trying to take Robin only to flip-flop  once again after seeing Luffy stand up  for her what becomes painfully clear  when we look at this example is how  conflicted Alka ji is between his own  idea of how to act morally and his duty  as a member of the Marines and the world  government as you might have suspected  all of this also plays a decisive role  in his sense of justice so now in order  to understand what lazy justice actually  means let's have a look at al-qaeda's  character arc to understand what Kooza  means when he talks about his lazy  justice we first have to understand how  his character has developed over the  course of the story  despite the admirals not exactly getting  a lot of screen time in the story Alka G  has nonetheless undergone a significant  change of perspective as a base for that  we have to look at the Admiral in his  younger days where he was actually still  a Vice Admiral to be more precise even  we have to look at the events  surrounding the destruction of the  island of O'Hara back in time okichi had  a very different take on justice in  general when first informed about the  events on the island by his men he  doesn't really care about the fate of  the islands for him it is simply the  deserved fate of criminals that have to  be taken out to protect the peace he  only changes his mind when he learns  that his old friend Jaguar D Seoul who  previously had deserted the Marines to  save Robins mother Livia is also on Hara  when arriving on the island he appears  indifferent to the injustice that is  happening there in the name of the 